WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.284
Last video ended on this curve,

00:00:02.865 --> 00:00:04.908
y equals three to the two x, and

00:00:04.948 --> 00:00:06.630
two other composites we haven't done yet.

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:09.788
Composites hide in everyday things.

00:00:10.353 --> 00:00:12.986
A drone hovers, and its camera tilts forward

00:00:13.027 --> 00:00:13.770
at a steady rate.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.398
The spot it films races ahead along the

00:00:16.439 --> 00:00:16.738
ground,

00:00:17.401 --> 00:00:19.224
and its speed comes from two places:

00:00:19.826 --> 00:00:21.348
how fast the camera tilts,

00:00:21.891 --> 00:00:23.854
and how far the spot moves for each

00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:24.616
bit of tilt.

00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:25.964
Keep that picture.

00:00:26.771 --> 00:00:28.639
Here are two quick answers for the derivative

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.006
of three to the two x.

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:32.965
One says two times three to the two

00:00:33.107 --> 00:00:33.227
x.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.499
The other says three to the two x,

00:00:35.681 --> 00:00:37.149
times the natural log of three.

00:00:38.113 --> 00:00:40.476
At x equals zero, the first predicts a

00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:42.920
slope of two, and the second about one

00:00:42.981 --> 00:00:43.822
point one zero.

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:45.912
Let's measure the real slope.

00:00:46.736 --> 00:00:49.844
Secants from closer and closer points give four,

00:00:50.286 --> 00:00:52.451
then about two point four six, then about

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:53.474
two point two two.

00:00:54.097 --> 00:00:56.025
They settle at about two point two.

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.075
Neither answer is right.

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:00.808
So what is the slope, and why does

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:02.576
a composite like this need more than one

00:01:02.637 --> 00:01:02.958
factor?

00:01:03.442 --> 00:01:04.274
Here's where it comes from.

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.386
Three to the two x is three squared,

00:01:07.627 --> 00:01:09.491
to the x, so it's nine to the

00:01:09.651 --> 00:01:09.772
x.

00:01:10.453 --> 00:01:12.477
And you know a to the x has

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.942
derivative a to the x, times the natural

00:01:15.003 --> 00:01:15.523
log of a.

00:01:16.287 --> 00:01:17.975
So the slope is nine to the x,

00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:19.663
times the natural log of nine.

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:22.495
The natural log of nine is two times

00:01:22.536 --> 00:01:23.479
the natural log of three.

00:01:24.102 --> 00:01:26.410
So the derivative is two, times the natural

00:01:26.451 --> 00:01:28.718
log of three, times three to the two

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:28.879
x.

00:01:29.704 --> 00:01:32.336
At zero, that's about two point two, the

00:01:32.357 --> 00:01:33.019
slope we measured.

00:01:33.925 --> 00:01:36.198
Each quick answer kept one factor and lost

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:36.561
the other.

00:01:37.145 --> 00:01:38.403
The picture shows why there are two.

00:01:39.148 --> 00:01:41.255
Three to the two x is three to

00:01:41.295 --> 00:01:43.865
the x, squashed sideways by a half.

00:01:44.547 --> 00:01:46.595
The base three gives the slope its natural

00:01:46.636 --> 00:01:47.257
log of three.

00:01:47.942 --> 00:01:50.417
The squash, from the inside two x, doubles

00:01:50.458 --> 00:01:50.518
it.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.644
So every composite needs two separate things:

00:01:54.265 --> 00:01:56.949
the outside's slope, worked out at the inside,

00:01:57.370 --> 00:01:58.952
and the inside's own slope.

00:01:59.635 --> 00:02:01.503
Here are the three outsides we haven't used

00:02:01.543 --> 00:02:01.704
yet.

00:02:02.545 --> 00:02:03.948
A to the power of an inside:

00:02:04.609 --> 00:02:06.632
copy it, times the natural log of a,

00:02:06.933 --> 00:02:08.435
times the inside's derivative.

00:02:09.218 --> 00:02:11.680
Log base a of an inside: the inside's

00:02:11.742 --> 00:02:14.185
derivative, over the inside times the natural log

00:02:14.206 --> 00:02:16.428
of a, and the inside must be positive.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.291
Tan of an inside:

00:02:18.812 --> 00:02:20.934
sec squared of the same inside, times the

00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:23.998
inside's derivative, and it breaks wherever the inside

00:02:24.059 --> 00:02:26.241
reaches pi over two, plus k pi.

00:02:26.943 --> 00:02:29.449
For the drone, the spot's distance is tan

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:31.556
of the tilt, so its speed is sec

00:02:31.597 --> 00:02:33.702
squared of the tilt, times the tilt's own

00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:34.023
rate.

00:02:34.526 --> 00:02:36.213
And once the tilt reaches pi over two,

00:02:36.515 --> 00:02:38.323
the camera sees only the horizon.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.531
The outside brings its own fixed part, the

00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:43.496
natural log of a, or sec squared.

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.709
The inside's derivative is an extra factor, and

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.698
the inside also decides the domain.

00:02:49.328 --> 00:02:51.174
Worked example one, from the course.

00:02:51.858 --> 00:02:55.324
Differentiate y equals log base three of, x

00:02:55.365 --> 00:02:57.748
squared plus one, and find the gradient at

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:58.730
x equals one.

00:02:59.453 --> 00:03:00.097
Domain first.

00:03:00.582 --> 00:03:03.048
The inside, x squared plus one, is always

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.154
at least one, so it's always positive.

00:03:05.638 --> 00:03:07.634
The function exists for every real x.

00:03:08.381 --> 00:03:10.214
The inside's derivative is two x.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.640
So d y by d x is two

00:03:12.782 --> 00:03:15.446
x, over x squared plus one, times the

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:16.508
natural log of three.

00:03:17.351 --> 00:03:20.038
At x equals one, that's two, over two

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.043
times the natural log of three, which is

00:03:22.345 --> 00:03:24.230
one over the natural log of three, about

00:03:24.331 --> 00:03:25.052
point nine one.

00:03:25.755 --> 00:03:27.719
And at x equals zero the top is

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.723
zero, so the curve is flat at its

00:03:29.825 --> 00:03:30.405
lowest point.

00:03:31.149 --> 00:03:32.175
Worked example two.

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:35.663
Differentiate y equals tan of e to the

00:03:35.885 --> 00:03:38.308
x, and say where the derivative exists.

00:03:39.071 --> 00:03:41.295
The inside is e to the x, and

00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:43.220
its derivative is e to the x as

00:03:43.281 --> 00:03:43.440
well.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.150
So d y by d x is e

00:03:46.172 --> 00:03:48.319
to the x, times sec squared of e

00:03:48.541 --> 00:03:49.022
to the x.

00:03:49.811 --> 00:03:50.457
Now the walls.

00:03:51.165 --> 00:03:53.951
Tan breaks where its inside equals pi over

00:03:54.032 --> 00:03:55.375
two, plus k pi.

00:03:55.937 --> 00:03:58.002
But e to the x is always positive,

00:03:58.365 --> 00:04:00.109
so it can only reach the positive ones:

00:04:00.491 --> 00:04:02.416
pi over two, three pi over two, and

00:04:02.457 --> 00:04:02.737
so on.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.406
So x can't be the natural log of

00:04:05.508 --> 00:04:07.594
pi over two, or the natural log of

00:04:07.615 --> 00:04:09.120
three pi over two, and so on.

00:04:09.804 --> 00:04:11.431
To the left, there are no walls at

00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:13.582
all, and the curve flattens towards zero.

00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:16.654
At x equals zero, the gradient is sec

00:04:16.695 --> 00:04:19.465
squared of one, about three point four three.

00:04:19.981 --> 00:04:21.672
Here's how to keep the constants in the

00:04:21.732 --> 00:04:22.376
right places.

00:04:23.321 --> 00:04:25.945
Powers multiply by the natural log of a,

00:04:26.787 --> 00:04:28.089
logs divide by it,

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:31.594
and the inside's slope always goes on top.

00:04:32.697 --> 00:04:35.386
Powers multiply, because a to the x is

00:04:35.587 --> 00:04:37.694
e to the power of, x times the

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:38.637
natural log of a.

00:04:39.721 --> 00:04:42.530
Logs divide, because log base a of x

00:04:42.972 --> 00:04:45.078
is the natural log of x, over the

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:45.841
natural log of a.

00:04:47.004 --> 00:04:49.771
And the inside's slope comes from the chain

00:04:49.811 --> 00:04:50.934
rule, every time.

00:04:51.899 --> 00:04:54.514
Try log base seven of, two x plus

00:04:54.554 --> 00:04:54.795
three.

00:04:55.438 --> 00:04:56.461
The two goes on top,

00:04:56.983 --> 00:04:59.251
and two x plus three, times the natural

00:04:59.272 --> 00:05:00.978
log of seven, goes underneath.

00:05:01.622 --> 00:05:03.957
Then check the domain the inside allows.

00:05:06.683 --> 00:05:07.087
Your turn.

00:05:07.771 --> 00:05:10.533
Find the exact gradient of the curve y

00:05:10.673 --> 00:05:12.975
equals five to the x squared, at the

00:05:13.015 --> 00:05:14.917
point where x equals one.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.414
Pause here to answer.

00:05:27.081 --> 00:05:29.105
The outside is five to the power of

00:05:29.145 --> 00:05:31.851
an inside, so copy it and multiply by

00:05:31.891 --> 00:05:33.234
the natural log of five.

00:05:33.936 --> 00:05:36.831
The inside is x squared, so multiply by

00:05:36.952 --> 00:05:37.977
two x as well.

00:05:38.739 --> 00:05:41.282
At x equals one, that's two, times the

00:05:41.322 --> 00:05:43.904
natural log of five, times five, which is

00:05:43.984 --> 00:05:45.886
ten times the natural log of five.

00:05:46.588 --> 00:05:48.753
Five times the natural log of five has

00:05:48.855 --> 00:05:50.459
dropped the inside's two x.

00:05:52.165 --> 00:05:52.511
Last one.

00:05:53.121 --> 00:05:56.850
Differentiate y equals log base two of, four

00:05:56.891 --> 00:05:58.895
minus x, and state its domain.

00:05:59.523 --> 00:06:00.316
Pause here to answer.

00:06:10.867 --> 00:06:11.667
Domain first:

00:06:12.248 --> 00:06:15.350
the inside must be positive, so four minus

00:06:15.511 --> 00:06:17.632
x is positive, and x is less than

00:06:17.693 --> 00:06:17.892
four.

00:06:18.695 --> 00:06:20.742
The inside's derivative is minus one.

00:06:21.405 --> 00:06:23.646
So d y by d x is minus

00:06:23.747 --> 00:06:26.788
one, over four minus x, times the natural

00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:28.950
log of two, for x less than four.

00:06:29.852 --> 00:06:31.956
Without the minus, the slope would be positive,

00:06:32.378 --> 00:06:35.083
but this log falls, because its inside shrinks

00:06:35.384 --> 00:06:36.085
as x grows.

00:06:37.754 --> 00:06:40.478
So for every composite, keep two factors, the

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.424
outside's slope at the inside and the inside's

00:06:43.705 --> 00:06:46.389
own slope, and let the inside decide the

00:06:46.411 --> 00:06:46.670
domain.

00:06:47.552 --> 00:06:49.473
If a question mixes these with a product

00:06:49.554 --> 00:06:52.316
or a quotient, find the last operation first,

00:06:52.477 --> 00:06:54.598
as before, and use these rules for the

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:55.599
pieces inside it.

00:06:56.222 --> 00:06:58.408
That finishes the derivatives you need for every

00:06:58.449 --> 00:06:59.792
function family in this strand.

00:07:00.496 --> 00:07:03.252
Next, we'll use these derivatives to build lines.

00:07:04.098 --> 00:07:07.045
Here's y equals cos two x, and the

00:07:07.086 --> 00:07:08.990
point where x equals pi over six.

00:07:09.673 --> 00:07:11.974
Its derivative is minus two sine two x,

00:07:12.315 --> 00:07:14.516
so the gradient there is minus root three.

00:07:15.399 --> 00:07:17.966
What line just touches the curve there, and

00:07:18.007 --> 00:07:19.772
what line meets it at right angles?

00:07:22.455 --> 00:07:23.297
Here are the key notes.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.468
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:25.509 --> 00:07:25.950
to copy them.
